//based on http://paulbourke.net/miscellaneous/interpolation/
//tension: 1 high, 0 normal, -1 low
//bias: 0 is even, positive is towards first segment, negative towards the other

THREE.Curve.Utils.hermiteInterpolate = function (p0, p1, p2, p3, t, tension, bias) {
	var m0 = (p1 - p0) * (1 + bias) * (1 - tension) / 2 
	       + (p2 - p1) * (1 - bias) * (1 - tension) / 2;

	var m1 = (p2 - p1) * (1 + bias) * (1 - tension) / 2 
	       + (p3 - p2) * (1 - bias) * (1 - tension) / 2;

	var t2 = t * t;
	var t3 = t2 * t;

	var h0 = 2 * t3 - 3 * t2 + 1;
	var h1 = t3 - 2 * t2 + t;
	var h2 = t3 - t2;
	var h3 = -2 * t3 + 3 * t2;

	return h0 * p1 + h1 * m0 + h2 * m1 + h3 * p2;
};

//based on SplineCurve3.js
//

THREE.HermiteCurve3 = THREE.Curve.create(
	function ( points, tension, bias ) { //custom curve constructor
		this.points = ( points == undefined ) ? [] : points;
		this.tension = ( tension == undefined ) ? 0.0 : tension;
		this.bias = ( bias == undefined ) ? 0.0 : bias;
	},

	function ( t ) { //getPoint: t is between 0-1

		var points = this.points;
		var point = ( points.length - 1 ) * t;

		var intPoint = Math.floor( point );
		var weight = point - intPoint;

		var point0 = points[ intPoint == 0 ? intPoint : intPoint - 1 ];
		var point1 = points[ intPoint ];
		var point2 = points[ intPoint > points.length - 2 ? points.length - 1 : intPoint + 1 ];
		var point3 = points[ intPoint > points.length - 3 ? points.length - 1 : intPoint + 2 ];

		var vector = new THREE.Vector3();

		vector.x = THREE.Curve.Utils.hermiteInterpolate( point0.x, point1.x, point2.x, point3.x, weight, this.tension, this.bias );
		vector.y = THREE.Curve.Utils.hermiteInterpolate( point0.y, point1.y, point2.y, point3.y, weight, this.tension, this.bias );
		vector.z = THREE.Curve.Utils.hermiteInterpolate( point0.z, point1.z, point2.z, point3.z, weight, this.tension, this.bias );

		return vector;
	}
);

content.thinking:
Now I understand the task. The app is a fly-through viewer — the "ship" is the splineCamera. The minimap should track the splineCamera position along the cameraSpline.

Design:

1. `Minimap` constructor: takes canvas element (220×220). Has:
   - `setTrack(curve)` — pre-sample 1024 points at t=i/1024 via `curve.getPoint(i/1024)` (note: HermiteCurve3 is not arc-length parameterized; getPointAt would use arc lengths. The camera uses getPointAt. For minimap shape, getPoint is fine, but for tracking the ship we use camera position anyway). Project x,z into Float32Array (2×1024 floats = 8KB). Compute bbox, uniform scale, offsets. Also compute tangents per sample (for dot-product filtering and low-speed arrow). Cache.
   - `reset()` — clear cache so it can be rebuilt (called on clear() or when track changes).
   - `update(position, velocity)` — find nearest sample index:
     - If have previous index: search window ±48 with wraparound.
     - Detect teleport/jump: if best distance in window is large (confidence low), or candidate direction opposes velocity... Spec: "腾空、复活导致位置跳变时，用速度方向与切线点积过滤反向候选，置信度不够才退化为一次粗粒度全搜". So: within window, among nearest candidates, filter by dot(velocity, tangent) — if velocity·tangent < 0 for the best candidate and speed is significant, mark low confidence → fall back to coarse full search (e.g. stride 8 over all 1024, then refine ±8). Only on low confidence, not every frame.
     - Actually simpler: compute windowed nearest; compute confidence = distance < threshold AND (speed low OR dot(vel, tangent) >= 0). If not confident → coarse full search (stride 4) + local refine. 
   - Arrow angle: if horizontal speed < threshold → use tangent at current index; else use atan2 of horizontal velocity.
   - `render()` — draw cached path (can pre-render path to offscreen canvas once per setTrack, then just drawImage + arrow each frame — avoids re-stroking 1024 points each frame).

2. Wire into Wipeout:
   - In `clear()`: `this.minimap.reset()` — actually minimap instance persists; reset clears track cache.
   - In `createCameraSpline`: after building cameraSpline, call `this.minimap.setTrack(this.cameraSpline)`.
   - In `animate()` fly branch: compute camera velocity (position - prevPosition)/dt, call `minimap.update(splineCamera.position, velocity)` then `minimap.render()`. Track prev position.

Where does Minimap live? Could be a separate file minimap.js, or appended in wipeout.js. The user says "由独立 Minimap 负责绘制" — independent Minimap class. And "改完先跑 node --check wipeout.js" — implies changes in wipeout.js. I'll create a separate `minimap.js` file and add script tag, plus wire in wipeout.js and index.html. But node --check wipeout.js — also check minimap.js. Either way. A separate file is cleaner; add `<script src="minimap.js"></script>` before wipeout.js.

Actually, to keep it simple and match "node --check wipeout.js", I could put Minimap in wipeout.js. But "独立 Minimap" just means independent class/module. I'll make minimap.js — cleaner. Hmm, but the verification step only mentions wipeout.js. I'll run node --check on both.

Canvas in index.html: fixed top-right, 220×220, `<canvas id="minimap" width="220" height="220">` with CSS position absolute top right, some margin, semi-transparent background, z-index above renderer canvas.

Velocity: in animate(), the fixed timestep loop may run multiple updateSplineCamera per frame. Compute velocity from splineCamera.position delta between frames: vel = (pos - prevPos) / dt. Store this.prevCameraPos.

Note camera damping: splineCamera.position is damped toward spline + 600y offset. Horizontal velocity is fine.

